<title>USA: U.S. Industries to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>U.S. Industries to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>ISELIN, N.J. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Industries said Thursday its board decided to buy back an additional $50 million of the company's shares.</p>
<p>The company said it had almost completed an earlier $100 million share buyback plan. As of June 6, the company had bought back 4.1 million shares for an amount of $99.9 million under the plan, it added.</p>
<p>Purchases under the share repurchase program are made from time to time, in the open market or privately, the company said. It added purchases are subject to restrictions applicable under its credit agreement and senior notes.</p>
